From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shiny <owner@shinychang.net>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:47:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: let Talk to Shy read the accessibility tree and run
 batches

- read_page with format "tree" lists the page's accessibility tree, one
  line per element with its role, name and state and a ref that click,
  type_text and scroll take; interactive: true keeps only what can be
  clicked or typed into.
- A ref is the element's backend node id, so the worker keeps no state
  for it, and it stops working once the element is gone.
- batch runs several tools in one call, stops at the first failure and
  logs each action in the panel.
- Input tools refuse a tab in the background, where clicks and keys never
  reach the page and a wheel event stalls the tab's debugger, and give
  up on input the page does not take within ten seconds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BYkQJUafT3hpFT1kBmDgzX
